Concept of Inheritance, Method overloading and Array of objects:
a. Create a class Room which will store the length and breadth of the room in two
variables. Create another class, Roomdemo, which will use the earlier class, and also
store the height of the room. Create instances of Roomdemo, set the values of length,
breadth and height of the room. Calculate the volume of the rooms.
b. Write a Java program to overload a function rect()
void rect (int, char): With one integer argument and one-character argument, draw a
filled square of side n using the character stored in ch.
void rect(int, int, char): With two integer arguments and one character argument, draw
a filled rectangle of length l and width b using characters stored in ch.
c. Declare a class Student that represents the following hierarchical information: ID,
name (First, Middle, Last), Gender, DOB (day, month, year), marks of 3 subjects
considering a 1D array (English, Mathematics, Computer Science). To store the name
and DOB, use the concept aggregation.
Write a Java program to store and display the database of n students by using an
array of objects. Also write methods to search a particular student (based on ID or
name) from the array and display his/her details.
